% An INLINE equation and a DISPLAYED one in the same document, which is what
% it takes to test that the two are told apart.
%
% A displayed equation is not a distinct construct in the box stream: what
% makes one displayed is that its paragraph holds nothing else. So the second
% `+p` below is one `${…}` and no prose, and the first has words around it —
% and every backend's display detection is that difference and nothing more
% (`markdown::para`'s `display_math`, `reflow::text`'s `sole_math_tex`).
%
% Kept apart from `math-selection.saty` rather than added to it: that fixture
% asserts an exact count of math runs, and a fourth would make it fail for a
% reason that has nothing to do with what it measures.

@require: stdja-mini
@require: math

document (|
  title = {Display and inline math};
  author = {yasuo};
|) '<
  +p { inline: ${\forall \epsilon} in a sentence. }
  +p { ${\sum_{k=1}^{n} k} }
>
